# Upstream benchmark payloads are immutable

The original OlympiadMAS benchmark payloads from `selinkaracaa/agent-olympiad`
`main` are **iron law**. Do not edit, reformat, rewrite paths, add fields, or
"sync" records inside the locked track directories.

## Locked paths (do not modify)

- `data/benchmarks/arml_local/`
- `data/benchmarks/arml_national_power/`
- `data/benchmarks/arml_national_team/`
- `data/benchmarks/arml_power/`
- `data/benchmarks/icpc/`
- `data/benchmarks/ieo_business_case/`
- `data/benchmarks/iiot/`
- `data/benchmarks/ijso_practical/`
- `data/benchmarks/ioaa_group/`
- `data/benchmarks/iol_team/`
- `data/benchmarks/jessup/`
- `data/benchmarks/wsc_writing/`

Also do not modify the corresponding original raw files that upstream already
shipped, unless the user explicitly asks to change a specific file. New
`runtime.json` manifests may be added beside those packs when they describe
availability without altering source material.

## What you may change

Only **our** additions:

- New tracks under `data/benchmarks/<new_id>/`
- `data/benchmarks/index.json` catalog metadata and entries; it is now the
  unified mixed-unit catalog. Do not use catalog edits to mutate locked payloads.
- New raw packs under `data/raw/<new_id>/`
- `from_zhongzheng/`, `data/viz/`, docs we own, extraction tooling outside those locked paths

## If a fix seems needed on a locked track

Stop and ask. Prefer putting corrected/extended data in a parallel new track or in `index_new` / staging — never silently patch the locked originals.
